  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "HQCCNN-BSTO: a hybrid quantum-classical CNN in which convolutional feature maps feed into a parameterized quantum layer; the Boosted Sooty Tern Optimization (BSTO) metaheuristic tunes hyperparameters. Applied to ransomware network-traffic classification using CICIDS2017 plus TLS traffic traces from GandCrab, Shade, Cryptowall, Cerber, WannaCry, Locky, Teslacrypt (Normal 20000; GandCrab 4172; Shade 1195; Cryptowall 1161; Cerber 569; WannaCry 453; Locky 340; Teslacrypt 285). Reports accuracy 99.7%, precision 99.5%, F1 99.5%, recall 99.4%, specificity 99.4%, error rate 0.01%, computation time 0.02 s. Baselines: RANSOMNET+, EDVT-MSSAN, Random Forest, Xception ColSeq, all substantially lower (85-90% range). Quantum layer is implemented as a noiseless simulated QCNN; no physical QPU reported.",
